@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Walking one served record back to the bytes it came from

left to right direction

rectangle "a served\nrecord" as R #fdf6f6
rectangle "the run\nrecord" as RUN
rectangle "the source\nregistry entry" as REG
rectangle "the archived\nbytes" as BYTES #fdf6f6

R -right-> RUN : run identifier
RUN -right-> REG : source name\nand version
REG -right-> BYTES : content hash

note bottom of R
  HOP 1 BREAKS. The record carries a run
  identifier only -- no snapshot hash and no
  build time. Two runs of the same source are
  indistinguishable from the record.
end note

note bottom of BYTES
  HOP 4 BREAKS. Two generations are retained.
  An older record reaches a hash whose bytes
  have been deleted.
end note

note as GOAL #fff4e5
  The target: a person with read access and no
  tooling walks this in four hops.
  Today hops 1 and 4 break, so the walk stops
  at the run and again at the archive.
end note
@enduml
